WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.029
(crowd hollering)

00:00:03.029 --> 00:00:05.953
- [Ross] Boxwars really
feels like a medieval battle.

00:00:05.953 --> 00:00:07.529
- [Crowd] Five, four.

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:08.665
- [Ross] The only difference
- [Crowd] Three, two.

00:00:08.665 --> 00:00:09.565
- [Ross] is it's with cardboard.

00:00:09.565 --> 00:00:11.626
- [Crowd] One, Boxwars!

00:00:11.626 --> 00:00:13.538
(crowd hollering)

00:00:13.538 --> 00:00:16.477
- [Ross] There's rules to
Boxwars, but they're very limited.

00:00:16.477 --> 00:00:18.515
- You will die! (grunts)

00:00:18.515 --> 00:00:19.348
- [Ross] There's no winners.

00:00:19.348 --> 00:00:21.134
We like to say that if
you're in a Boxwars,

00:00:21.134 --> 00:00:22.536
(screams)

00:00:22.536 --> 00:00:24.843
you've already lost.

00:00:24.843 --> 00:00:26.107
(growling)

00:00:26.107 --> 00:00:27.454
(laughter)

00:00:27.454 --> 00:00:28.935
(upbeat music)

00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:32.947
- I'm Ross, I'm one of the
supreme overlords of Boxwars.

00:00:32.947 --> 00:00:36.985
Boxwars is a collective of
people that love to get together,

00:00:36.985 --> 00:00:38.558
create cardboard creations,

00:00:38.558 --> 00:00:42.591
and then destroy them in an epic battle.

00:00:42.591 --> 00:00:45.617
It's more about competitiveness
in being creative.

00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:49.196
The only materials that
you can use are cardboard,

00:00:49.196 --> 00:00:51.499
adhesives like tape, hot glue.

00:00:51.499 --> 00:00:53.175
Whatever you can find in packaging,

00:00:53.175 --> 00:00:56.614
that's the stuff that we like
to use to build our suits.

00:00:56.614 --> 00:00:58.933
Every single battle has a
new engineering challenge,

00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:00.692
like building a giant aircraft carrier,

00:01:00.692 --> 00:01:02.689
or building a monster
truck that actually rolls,

00:01:02.689 --> 00:01:04.546
or a train, which has to carry in

00:01:04.546 --> 00:01:06.725
a whole bunch of policemen.

00:01:06.725 --> 00:01:09.001
We encourage people to
come down to our events

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:12.738
and build as elaborate costumes
as they can possibly make.

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:15.742
Once they've built the props,
then we all gather at a park,

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.216
and then, we battle.

00:01:17.216 --> 00:01:20.649
Everyone comes in and clashes
and destroys everything.

00:01:20.649 --> 00:01:21.905
(grunts)

00:01:21.905 --> 00:01:23.860
Stuff that we've spent weeks on designing,

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.967
(wailing)
it's all gone in seconds.

00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:27.806
(chill music)
We just started off

00:01:27.806 --> 00:01:31.327
really small, but then, all
of a sudden, it blew up.

00:01:31.327 --> 00:01:32.475
There's generally around about

00:01:32.475 --> 00:01:34.934
50 to 100 people in the actual battle,

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:38.556
and then it can be hundreds
and hundreds of spectators.

00:01:38.556 --> 00:01:40.474
We've got chapters that have started up

00:01:40.474 --> 00:01:41.424
all around the world.

00:01:41.424 --> 00:01:43.330
We've had groups in Japan, in Europe,

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.734
in America, in Canada.

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:47.180
It seems so childish,

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.818
but it's fantastic that
a concept like this

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:52.868
crosses cultural and language barriers.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.744
Boxwars is based around comedy.

00:01:54.744 --> 00:01:55.577
(laughter)

00:01:55.577 --> 00:01:57.690
That's the whole point
of Boxwars, we're losers.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.364
What we're doing is quite pathetic.

00:01:59.364 --> 00:02:00.556
We should all have real jobs,

00:02:00.556 --> 00:02:03.286
but here we are building
stuff out of cardboard.

00:02:03.286 --> 00:02:05.674
If you laugh at us, that's
exactly what we want.

00:02:05.674 --> 00:02:07.757
(growls)

00:02:09.296 --> 00:02:10.530
Alright, that's pretty pathetic.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.780
(laughter)

